              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An agent runs 10 steps, each adding about 1k tokens to the history. Roughly how many input tokens are billed in total?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "About ==55k==, not 10k: step n resends n×1k tokens.",
                "Input grows quadratically with steps, so cut history and cache the prefix."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Caching is on, but cache_read_tokens is always 0. The system prompt starts with `Now: {timestamp}`. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Caching needs an exact prefix, and the timestamp changes it on every request.",
                "Move volatile text to the end, after the stable prefix."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Small model costs 1, large costs 10, and 95% of steps escalate. Does the cascade save money?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: 1 + 0.95×10 = ==10.5==, above always-large at 10.",
                "Small always runs, so a high escalation rate loses money."
